ALGORITHM ORIGINALITY AND ATTRIBUTION NOTICE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The statistical and machine-learning algorithms implemented in the Rust core
(core-rust/) are ORIGINAL implementations written from public mathematical
formulas. No third-party statistical/machine-learning library is linked.

The following are standard published methods; their implementation here is
original code, not a copy of any specific library or project:

  * Kolmogorov-Smirnov two-sample test (core-rust/src/stats/ks.rs)
      - Classical non-parametric test (Kolmogorov 1933; Smirnov 1939).
  * Lomb-Scargle periodogram (core-rust/src/stats/lomb.rs)
      - Classic spectral analysis for unevenly sampled data
        (Lomb 1976; Scargle 1982).
  * Kullback-Leibler divergence (core-rust/src/stats/kl.rs)
      - Information-theoretic divergence (Kullback & Leibler 1951).
  * Shannon entropy (core-rust/src/stats/entropy.rs)
      - Classical information entropy (Shannon 1948).
  * Isolation Forest (core-rust/src/iforest.rs)
      - Anomaly detection via isolation trees
        (Liu, Ting, Zhou, "Isolation Forest", ICDM 2008).
        The inference engine (flat node arrays, INT8-quantized weights,
        recursion-free traversal) is original implementation.

Design inspiration and research background (acknowledged with thanks):

  * Academic papers on accelerometer/IMU-based privacy attacks that informed
    the threat model and detection rationale:
      - Spearphone (NDSS 2020)
      - AccelEve (SenSys 2019)
      - EarSpy (2022)
  * Open-source engineering references for store-listing copy and background
    service strategy (no code copied):
      - Access Dots
      - PilferShush Jammer
      - TrackerControl

No code from the above projects has been copied into this repository.

